                <pb facs="0435" n="327" sameAs="frus:frus1927v02/pg327"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.113/1061: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in China</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">MacMurray</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-12-23T18:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">December 23,
                                1927—6 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>429. Your 1122, December 23, 7 p.m. Department agrees with you that tear gas
                    comes within scope of arms embargo and you should instruct Consul at Canton
                    accordingly.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
